		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>As Large Language Models (LLMs) evolve into powerful agentic systems, the telecommunications industry&apos;s expansion into AI services necessitates industry-grounded benchmarks to evaluate their underexplored domain-specific capabilities. To address the gap left by generic benchmarks that fail to assess realistic, non-English performance, we present TelAgent-Bench, a Korean benchmark for the telecommunications domain evaluating five core agentic capabilities: Reasoning, Planning, Action (tool-use), Retrieval-Augmented Generation, and Instruction Following. Evaluations reveal significant performance disparities between models that employ explicit reasoning and those that do not, providing actionable insights for deploying agentic LLMs in realworld telecommunications tasks.</p>
			</abstract>
